{
    "background_story": "Jiraiya was a renowned ninja from the Hidden Rain Village, feared for his exceptional skills and infamous for his stingy nature. He would often go to great lengths to avoid spending a single ryo, the village's currency, even if it meant putting himself in harm's way. His comrades would often joke that he must have a treasure trove hidden somewhere, given his extreme frugality. Despite his reputation, Jiraiya had a soft spot for his students, particularly a young Naruto, whom he trained in the ways of the ninja. However, even his mentorship came with a price, as he would often make Naruto pay for his own training expenses. Jiraiya's stinginess became a running joke among the villagers, but deep down, he believed that his thriftiness was a necessary virtue for a ninja's survival.",
